e identification for Measurement MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"Measurement\", \"software_version\": \"1.3.0\", \"crc_checksum\": \"A6C913AF\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Measurement MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"4G\", \"software_version\": \"1.2.0\", \"crc_checksum\": \"AE3D9862\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Communication MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"4G\", \"software_version\": \"1.3.0\", \"crc_checksum\": \"3B33D2C8\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Communication MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"4G\", \"software_version\": \"1.3.1\", \"crc_checksum\": \"FDE7CBB6\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Communication MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"NB-IoT\", \"software_version\": \"1.3.0\", \"crc_checksum\": \"E5742163\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Communication MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"NB-IoT\", \"software_version\": \"1.3.1\", \"crc_checksum\": \"EC4FF9C6\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Communication MCU\"},\n{\"software_group\": \"NB-IoT\", \"software_version\": \"1.3.2\", \"crc_checksum\": \"C8CABC2D\", \"remark\": \"Software identification for Communication MCU\"}\n\ndescription: \"Software versions grouped by MCU function: Measurement and Communication (4G and NB-IoT).\"\nfootnotes: [\"[1]\"]? The footnotes field in matrix_tables presumably holds footnote texts. I'll put footnotes: [\"[1] The software version and checksum are displayed on the meter during the circular sequence every 10 minutes. The software version and checksum are displayed sequentially with first for the Measurement part then the Communications part.\"] — or reference marker only. Since global footnotes[] will have the full text, here I can put the marker \"[1]\". Hmm, ambiguous. I'll put the marker reference \"[1]\" in the table's footnotes array and full text in global footnotes. Actually, maybe better to just put full text in global footnotes and set table footnotes: [\"[1]\"]. Fine.\n\nGlobal footnotes: